2. Layer 7 - Application Layer
What is it?

This is the layer where the user interacts with the network.

Whenever you open:

Google Chrome
Firefox
Outlook
WhatsApp Web
SSH Terminal

You are using the Application Layer.

This layer provides services to applications.


Protocols
HTTP
HTTPS
FTP
SSH
DNS
SMTP
Example

You type:

https://github.com

The browser sends an HTTP/HTTPS request.

Application Layer starts the communication.

==> Real Life Example

Imagine ordering food from Zomato.

You only press

Order Now

You don't care how food reaches you.

Application Layer is exactly like that.

==> In Linux
curl google.com

or

wget https://example.com

These commands work at the Application Layer.

3. Layer 6 - Presentation Layer
What is it?

This layer is responsible for

Formatting data
Encryption
Decryption
Compression

It makes sure both computers understand the data.

==> SSL/TLS

When you open

https://google.com

The browser encrypts data using

SSL/TLS.

That happens here.

==> Real Life Example

Suppose you send a gift.

Before sending,

you wrap it nicely.

Wrapping the gift is like Presentation Layer.


4. Layer 5 - Session Layer
What is it?

This layer creates,

maintains,

and closes communication between two devices.

Think of it as managing the conversation.

==> Example

Suppose you SSH into a Linux server.

ssh user@192.168.1.10

A session starts.

While working,

the session stays active.

When you type

exit

The session ends.

==> Real Life Example

Phone call.

Call starts.

Conversation happens.

Call ends.

Exactly what Session Layer does.

5. Layer 4 - Transport Layer
What is it?

Transport Layer is responsible for

Delivering data
Error checking
Reliability
Data segmentation

It decides how data should travel.

There are two protocols.

A)TCP Transmission Control Protocol

it has its features:-
Reliable
Connection-oriented
Slow

==> How TCP Works

a) Computer A says

Can I send data?

Computer B replies

Yes

Data starts transferring.

If one packet is lost,

TCP sends it again.

Nothing gets lost.

*****

Used By
HTTP
HTTPS
SSH
FTP

********

==> Example

Downloading Ubuntu ISO.

If one packet is missing,

TCP downloads it again.

File never gets corrupted.

b) Real Life Example

Courier Service

If the parcel is missing,

company sends another parcel.

Reliable.

B) UDP - User Datagram Protocol

Fast
Connectionless
No guarantee.

Example

Watching YouTube Live.

One packet is lost.

Video continues.

Nobody waits.

********

Used By
Video calls
Gaming
DNS
Streaming

Real Life Example

FM Radio

If one word is missed,

the program continues.

**********

