7. Layer 2 - Data Link Layer
What is it?

Responsible for communication inside the same network.

Uses

MAC Address
Switch
ARP


==> MAC Address

Every network card has a unique hardware address.

Example

08:00:27:AA:BB:CC

==> Switch

Switch sends data only to the correct device.

Unlike Hub,

it doesn't send data everywhere.

Example

Office LAN

20 computers connected.

Switch sends data only to the destination computer.

==> ARP

ARP means

Address Resolution Protocol.

It converts

IP Address

↓

MAC Address

Linux Example
arp -a

it shows ip and mac address

==> Real Life Example

You know your friend's name,

but not his house.

You ask neighbours.

ARP works similarly.

It asks

"Who has this IP?"

The device replies

"This is my MAC Address."

