9. Complete Example (How Google Opens)

You type:

www.google.com
Application Layer – Browser creates an HTTPS request.
Presentation Layer – Data is encrypted using SSL/TLS.
Session Layer – Starts and manages the communication session.
Transport Layer – TCP breaks the data into packets and ensures reliable delivery.
Network Layer – Router forwards packets based on IP addresses.
Data Link Layer – Switch delivers frames using MAC addresses within the local network.


The server processes the request, and the response comes back through the same layers in reverse order.
Physical Layer – Bits travel through Ethernet cable or Wi-Fi signals.
